    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a condensed schedule today, leaving us to rely on a core group led by **Sam Antonacci**, whose score of 63.61 makes him our premier start. **Sam Antonacci** benefits significantly from batting leadoff against Kumar Rocker; while the opposing xERA of 4.36 is league-average, the combination of his top-of-the-order placement and a favorable platoon advantage provides the highest floor on the roster today. **Nasim Nunez** follows closely with a 59.76 rating; despite hitting in the bottom-third of the lineup, he faces the most exploitable matchup of the day in Feltner (5.10 xERA). The matchup against Feltner provides the necessary SP weakness for **Nasim Nunez** to hunt for high-value stolen base opportunities, a critical priority for our league standing.\n\n**Miguel Vargas** (55.00) remains a solid, if unspectacular, play in the #3 hole. His projections are bolstered by a high xwOBA of 0.389, though he faces moderate resistance from Kumar Rocker. We are keeping a close watch on **Jackson Merrill**, whose 51.66 score is contingent on the final lineup verification; should he be moved out of the #5 spot, his efficiency could fluctuate. It was a quiet day for our stars, as **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** are all unavailable due to scheduled off-days, forcing us to lean heavily on our depth. We considered elevating **Heliot Ramos** or **Jordan Westburg** from the reserves to hedge against the volatility of the bottom-order hitters, but the current projected efficiency for **Nasim Nunez** specifically against the vulnerable Feltner edged them out of the starting slots. Ensure monitoring of the lineup for **Jackson Merrill**, as any drastic shift in his batting position will necessitate a re-evaluation of his status against Braxton Ashcraft.",
